{"agent":"bugs-review-tooling","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"The `model` property description was rewritten from \"Model that performed it\" to \"REVIEWER's model\", while the sibling `reviewer_model` is documented as \"Like `model`; says it IS the reviewer.\" Those two descriptions contradict each other, and the handler only sets the reviewer assertion from the `reviewer_model` key:\n\n- `model=a.get(\"reviewer_model\", \"\") or a.get(\"model\", \"\") or \"\"`\n- `model_is_reviewer=bool(a.get(\"reviewer_model\"))`\n\nAn MCP client that follows the schema literally passes the reviewer's model as `model` (as the description now instructs). That call sets `model_is_reviewer=False`, i.e. the value is treated as a non-reviewer model. Two consequences: when the reviewer model is in the author's family, gate record's reviewer-gate check refuses it (exit 3 / error) even though the client used the field the tool told it to use; and even when it is accepted, the resulting record cannot distinguish a reviewer model from an author model, defeating the point of fix B1979dac602. The `model` description should not assert reviewer-ness, or `model_is_reviewer` should be derived from it as well.","digest":"25a5a83adf42f6b6","location":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (gate_record schema, `model` property + `model_is_reviewer` derivation)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (gate_record schema, `model` property + `model_is_reviewer` derivation)"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"`_git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"main\")` hard-codes the primary branch name. The repo is created by `run_cli(repo, \"init\")`; on any environment where the default branch is `master` (git's historical default when `init.defaultBranch` is unset, still common in older git/CI images), no `main` ref exists. Then `subprocess.run(..., check=True)` raises `CalledProcessError` and the test errors instead of exercising the refusal path. The test should derive the primary checkout's head without naming the branch (e.g. `_git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")`, which is exactly the wrong sha the B1 bug was about, or resolve the current branch with `--abbrev-ref HEAD`).","digest":"745c417102b9d4a5","location":"tests/test_review_gate_integrity.py::test_a_reviewed_sha_that_is_not_the_branch_head_is_refused","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_review_gate_integrity.py::test_a_reviewed_sha_that_is_not_the_branch_head_is_refused"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":29407,"diff_sha":"282137d08363549bcebd1062dd44238b44949c08659c1c4b3c03849eddfbe842","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-review-tooling-integrity","elapsed_s":533.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py (gate_record schema, `model` property + `model_is_reviewer` derivation)","tests/test_review_gate_integrity.py::test_a_reviewed_sha_that_is_not_the_branch_head_is_refused"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e621823c87fb392f4e5f94ba0","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":11074,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-review-tooling-integrity","ts":"2026-10-02T18:42:29.465481Z"}
