{"agent":"bugs-review-tooling","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_reviewed_sha_check` resolves the caller-supplied value with `W.rev(where, sha)` where `where` is the item's **worktree** whenever the worktree exists. `W.rev` is a ref-resolving helper (the same function is used on `it.branch`, a branch name), so it happily resolves symbolic refs — including `HEAD`. That means the exact documented trigger of B1ed2b4fde6 is no longer caught: `roborev review HEAD` run from an item's worktree enqueued the *primary's* HEAD (the review really saw `main`), but if the gate record is made with `--reviewed-sha HEAD`, `W.rev(wt, \"HEAD\")` returns the *worktree's* HEAD, i.e. the item's branch head, so `full == head` and the sha is accepted and recorded as \"reviewed\" with no warning or refusal. Concretely: item worktree exists, branch head is `abc…`, primary head is `def…`; `gate record --reviewed-sha HEAD` stores `abc…` as reviewed even though the review was of `def…`, which is precisely the \"review of main recorded against the item\" failure the change claims to fix. Resolving against `repo` (with the explicit-sha contract) or refusing non-hex values is needed to actually block this input.","digest":"89e40a1acb6bced5","location":"ddflow/api/gates.py `_reviewed_sha_check` (`where = wt …` / `W.rev(where, sha)`)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/gates.py `_reviewed_sha_check` (`where = wt …` / `W.rev(where, sha)`)"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":29407,"diff_sha":"282137d08363549bcebd1062dd44238b44949c08659c1c4b3c03849eddfbe842","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-review-tooling-integrity","elapsed_s":579.9,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"R