{"agent":"bugs-review-tooling","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new guard hardcodes the length range of a SHA-1 object name. Git supports SHA-256 object-format repositories (`git init --object-format=sha256`), where `git rev-parse HEAD` yields a 64-character hex commit id. In such a repository the regex `[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}` fails `fullmatch` on a perfectly valid commit sha, so `resolve_reviewed_sha` returns the \"not a commit sha\" refusal and `gate record <id> standards --reviewed-sha <64-hex-sha>` is rejected with exit 3 even though the sha is exactly the item's branch head. This is the same class of environment the change is trying to protect against (valid input refused), just for a different object format; the upper bound should be `{7,64}` (or `{7,}` with a later `W.rev` validation).","digest":"6140b0f89ee52442","location":"ddflow/api/gates.py:477 (`re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}\", sha)`)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/gates.py:477 (`re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}\", sha)`)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":6261,"diff_sha":"d8f2698db623439ae53214c1b96303fdc679920ca6cc0ad8d7cac2ab50be8062","diff_source":"commit c2b0991fecee vs its first parent","elapsed_s":121.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/gates.py:477 (`re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}\", sha)`)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e2fcb32638e043835a87ebce9","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":11162,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-review-tooling-integrity","ts":"2026-10-02T18:50:40.287911Z"}
